From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Sync to Exact Content Framerate: timed with vsync off, locked when it cannot fit

Two things for a variable refresh display.

With Sync to Exact Content Framerate, the runloop's timer paces every
frame, and a context that times its presents (0014, 0018) shows each one
at its own time. Vsync off then has nothing left to switch off: it only
made video presents non-blocking, which shows a frame whenever it happens
to be ready. On a variable refresh panel that is a refresh of that
length, below the panel's range for a 60 Hz game. Video now stays
blocking under Sync to Exact Content Framerate, at init and when the
nonblock state is applied. Fast-forward still presents without blocking.

A frame is shown for a whole number of refreshes, each no shorter than
the display's fastest. Content that does not fit twice into the display's
rate, such as the few arcade boards at 60.1 to 61 Hz against 120.198,
has no multiple in range. For that session, drivers_init turns Sync to
Exact Content Framerate off and vsync on before the swap interval is
chosen. The content is then locked to half the display's rate, with
audio resampled, as on a fixed refresh display.

Measured on SM8550 (Retroid Pocket Nova), VRR on: Super Mario World,
vsync off, 3606 refreshes for 1803 frames in 30 s, none longer than
8.42 ms. The same forced onto the 119.88 Hz mode: "60.099 fps does not
fit twice", swap interval 2, the audio rate adjusted to 59.94 frames a
second, 2398 refreshes in 20 s, none longer than 8.46 ms.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
diff --git a/gfx/video_driver.c b/gfx/video_driver.c
--- a/gfx/video_driver.c
+++ b/gfx/video_driver.c
@@ -5680,7 +5680,14 @@
    video.height                      = height;
    video.fullscreen                  = settings->bools.video_fullscreen
          || ((uint32_t)retro_atomic_load_relaxed_int(&video_st->flags) & VIDEO_FLAG_FORCE_FULLSCREEN);
-   video.vsync                       = settings->bools.video_vsync
+   /* With Sync to Exact Content Framerate the runloop's timer paces
+    * every frame, and a context that times its presents shows each at
+    * its own time: vsync off has nothing left to switch off. Presenting
+    * without blocking would only show a frame whenever it happened to be
+    * ready, which on a variable refresh display is a refresh that long.
+    * Fast-forward still presents without blocking. */
+   video.vsync                       = (settings->bools.video_vsync
+            || settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable)
          && !settings->bools.video_scanline_sync
          && (!(runloop_st->flags & RUNLOOP_FLAG_FORCE_NONBLOCK));
    video.force_aspect                = settings->bools.video_force_aspect;
diff --git a/retroarch.c b/retroarch.c
--- a/retroarch.c
+++ b/retroarch.c
@@ -1578,7 +1578,10 @@
       if (video_st->current_video->set_nonblock_state)
       {
          bool video_nonblock        = enable;
-         if (!video_vsync || runloop_force_nonblock)
+         /* Not with Sync to Exact Content Framerate: see video.vsync in
+          * video_driver_init_internal(). */
+         if (     (!video_vsync && !settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable)
+               || runloop_force_nonblock)
             video_nonblock = true;
          video_st->current_video->set_nonblock_state(video_st->data,
                video_nonblock,
@@ -1625,6 +1628,26 @@
 
    DRIVER_FLAGS_NORMALIZE(flags);
 
+   /* Sync to Exact Content Framerate on a variable refresh display shows
+    * each frame for a whole number of refreshes, each no shorter than the
+    * display's fastest: twice for 45 to 60 Hz content on a 120 Hz panel.
+    * Content that does not fit twice into the display's rate - a few
+    * arcade boards run at 60.1 to 61 Hz against 120.198 - has no multiple
+    * in range. Lock it to the display instead, as on a fixed refresh
+    * display: vsync, and the core's rate adjusted to half the display's.
+    * For this session; the next launch sets both again. */
+   if (     settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable
+         && video_st->av_info.timing.fps > 0.0
+         && settings->floats.video_refresh_rate > 0.0f
+         && video_st->av_info.timing.fps * 2.0
+            > (double)settings->floats.video_refresh_rate * 1.0001)
+   {
+      RARCH_LOG("[Video] %.3f fps does not fit twice into %.3f Hz, locked to the display.\n",
+            video_st->av_info.timing.fps, settings->floats.video_refresh_rate);
+      settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable = false;
+      settings->bools.video_vsync        = true;
+   }
+
    /* Content av_info based automatic swap interval must be set early. */
    runloop_set_video_swap_interval(settings);
 
